WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.842
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.112 --> 00:09.114
[theme music playing]

3
00:30.135 --> 00:32.012
[mysterious music playing]

4
00:32.096 --> 00:33.889
[whirring]

5
00:33.973 --> 00:34.974
[breathes shakily]

6
00:40.896 --> 00:42.022
[hissing]

7
00:42.648 --> 00:43.649
Get down.

8
00:48.028 --> 00:50.072
-I said get down. -What?

9
00:51.448 --> 00:52.783
Get down!

10
01:02.626 --> 01:04.128
What the sh…

11
01:06.547 --> 01:07.923
That scared me!

12
01:19.226 --> 01:20.769
It's all right now.

13
01:21.478 --> 01:22.605
It's over.

14
01:30.863 --> 01:33.532
-[Song-yi gasps] -Easy. Get up slowly.

15
01:33.616 --> 01:35.200
Your muscles are in shock.

16
01:37.745 --> 01:38.746
[grunts]

17
01:38.829 --> 01:40.956
[groaning]

18
01:44.251 --> 01:45.544
Thank you for this.

19
01:45.628 --> 01:48.797
Wait. What on earth just happened?

20
01:48.881 --> 01:51.008
The fire suppression sprinkler exploded.

21
01:51.842 --> 01:53.302
It must have been defective.

22
01:54.219 --> 01:56.931
Even the cheapest ones shouldn't explode like that.

23
01:57.932 --> 01:59.016
What brand is it?

24
01:59.099 --> 02:00.893
Was it installed quite a while ago?

25
02:02.019 --> 02:04.438
You haven't noticed anything unusual about it?

26
02:05.898 --> 02:06.899
[breathes shakily]

27
02:06.982 --> 02:09.443
Well, I'm not really sure actually.

28
02:10.444 --> 02:11.737
When did we install it?

29
02:12.404 --> 02:13.697
About six months ago?

30
02:14.698 --> 02:16.492
We were a little short on cash,

31
02:17.117 --> 02:19.244
-so we got a bootleg. -Hmm?

32
02:19.828 --> 02:21.789
Did you say "bootleg"?

33
02:23.874 --> 02:25.626
[Du-yeong] Hey, Song-yi.

34
02:27.211 --> 02:28.754
Someone just came in.

35
02:36.220 --> 02:40.474
I don't know how to thank you for coming all this way to visit our restaurant.

36
02:41.183 --> 02:43.686
But I am terribly sorry, ma'am.

37
02:44.895 --> 02:47.106
There's been an unexpected issue in the kitchen,

38
02:47.189 --> 02:49.483
so I'm afraid we won't be able to serve dinner tonight.

39
02:50.109 --> 02:51.318
[sighs]

40
02:51.402 --> 02:54.279
[Song-yi] Again, I'm sorry for all the trouble.

41
02:59.118 --> 03:01.036
[stammers] I heard something explode.

42
03:01.120 --> 03:03.539
Is everything all right? Should we call emergency services?

43
03:03.622 --> 03:05.374
Oh, don't worry.

44
03:05.457 --> 03:06.959
Everything's fine now.

45
03:07.042 --> 03:09.044
The staff is cleaning up the mess inside.

46
03:09.128 --> 03:10.754
[sighs] That's a relief.

47
03:11.630 --> 03:14.675
Um, I don't know exactly what happened,

48
03:14.758 --> 03:17.094
but is there absolutely no way you can cook?

49
03:17.177 --> 03:20.472
We have a guest who made a long trip just to dine at Famiglia again

50
03:20.556 --> 03:23.017
after a very long time.

51
03:23.976 --> 03:25.019
[sighs]

52
03:25.769 --> 03:26.770
Please.

53
03:27.354 --> 03:28.522
I'd really appreciate it.

54
03:29.732 --> 03:31.608
It's been ten years.

55
03:38.282 --> 03:39.658
I'm so… [inhales sharply]

56
03:41.035 --> 03:43.245
I'm really, really sorry, mister.

57
03:46.457 --> 03:49.835
Especially if you used to love our food so much…

58
03:52.337 --> 03:55.132
then I really don't think we can serve you tonight.

59
03:56.216 --> 03:57.968
Please understand.

60
03:58.052 --> 04:00.929
Serving you subpar food in a situation like this

61
04:01.013 --> 04:03.390
would dishonor my father's memory.

62
04:03.474 --> 04:04.558
[sniffles]

63
04:09.104 --> 04:10.355
Oh, dear. [sighs]

64
04:12.900 --> 04:13.901
[sighs]

65
04:13.984 --> 04:16.570
[Henri] I just miss Chef Choi's food.

66
04:17.863 --> 04:19.448
It's unfortunate.

67
04:20.783 --> 04:22.993
But I do understand.

68
04:25.162 --> 04:27.664
It's a shame, but I understand as well.

69
04:28.874 --> 04:29.875
[sighs]

70
04:29.958 --> 04:32.294
[Jeong-won] I think we should head back for today.

71
04:33.545 --> 04:34.630
Henri Bernier?

72
04:35.964 --> 04:37.674
What is he doing here?

73
04:38.967 --> 04:40.302
Who?

74
04:40.385 --> 04:41.386
Henri who?

75
04:42.137 --> 04:44.181
-[screaming] -[loud clattering]

76
04:44.264 --> 04:46.141
[Song-yi gasping]

77
04:46.225 --> 04:48.102
Hey, are you okay?

78
04:48.185 --> 04:49.937
What is this, a battlefield?

79
04:50.020 --> 04:53.148
-[Du-yeong groaning] Hang on. -Hey, are you all right?

80
04:53.232 --> 04:55.818
-Easy. Easy. Easy. -[Du-yeong] Ow.

81
04:55.901 --> 04:57.402
-[whimpers] -Easy.

82
04:57.486 --> 04:58.904
Oh, my God. Did you hit your head?

83
04:58.987 --> 05:00.614
-Yeah. -Let me see.

84
05:02.658 --> 05:03.659
Is it bleeding?

85
05:06.036 --> 05:07.746
[breathing deeply]

86
05:07.830 --> 05:08.831
Are you okay?

87
05:11.125 --> 05:12.668
Yes, I'm fine.

88
05:13.210 --> 05:14.294
I'm okay, really.

89
05:15.003 --> 05:16.255
[sighs]

90
05:18.257 --> 05:19.258
Thank you so much.

91
05:29.893 --> 05:32.855
Goodness! I didn't expect anything like this.

92
05:32.938 --> 05:35.232
Well, why don't we just head straight to Exception?

93
05:35.315 --> 05:36.775
We can have a glass of wine there.

94
05:36.859 --> 05:38.402
[sighs] No, thank you.

95
05:39.653 --> 05:41.989
Hearing about Chef Choi Seung-hyo today

96
05:42.614 --> 05:43.782
has really weighed on me.

97
05:45.325 --> 05:47.744
I just arrived today, so I'm tired as well.

98
05:48.912 --> 05:50.914
[sighs] Perhaps some other time.

99
05:51.498 --> 05:54.334
It's been a long time since I've seen Chef Cha Woo-jin.

100
05:54.418 --> 05:57.379
I'd like to rest before I have a glass of wine with him.

101
05:58.255 --> 06:00.799
Well, if that's what you want, no problem.

102
06:02.092 --> 06:04.303
I can catch a taxi across the street.

103
06:05.929 --> 06:08.599
Thank you for coming to pick me up, Ms. Baek.

104
06:08.682 --> 06:11.351
And thank you for trying.

105
06:11.435 --> 06:12.436
[chuckles]

106
06:13.020 --> 06:16.440
In that case, I'll have your luggage sent to your hotel.

107
06:17.441 --> 06:18.442
Thank you so much.

108
06:27.034 --> 06:31.288
[sighs] Why did everything have to fall apart at the last minute, darling?

109
06:31.371 --> 06:34.208
And on the very first day, our most important guest arrives.

110
06:34.291 --> 06:35.584
I swear,

111
06:35.667 --> 06:39.254
nothing ever goes right whenever Famiglia is involved, nothing!

112
06:40.589 --> 06:41.590
[sighs]

113
06:41.673 --> 06:43.759
[clicks tongue] It's like I say, you know,

114
06:43.842 --> 06:46.011
there are two types of people in this world.

115
06:47.137 --> 06:49.598
People who make the impossible possible,

116
06:50.891 --> 06:53.185
and people who make the possible impossible.

117
06:55.395 --> 06:56.396
[gasps]

118
06:56.480 --> 06:59.066
Did you see that girl's face? The way it's bunched together?

119
06:59.149 --> 07:01.860
She looks just like her father, and I bet she's just as stubborn.

120
07:01.944 --> 07:05.405
Oh! This is going to be a nightmare.

121
07:05.489 --> 07:08.909
[exclaims] It's my brain, it hurts.

122
07:08.992 --> 07:11.453
Where are my antacids? And why isn't he here yet?

123
07:12.079 --> 07:14.414
What? Who? Henri Bernier?

124
07:14.498 --> 07:16.541
You mean that man who came in earlier

125
07:16.625 --> 07:18.752
was actually the world-famous chef Henri Bernier?

126
07:18.835 --> 07:20.337
[sighs]

127
07:21.255 --> 07:22.256
[sighs]

128
07:27.386 --> 07:29.096
Of all days, why today?

129
07:29.179 --> 07:30.722
[sighs]

130
07:32.015 --> 07:35.060
He said it's been ten years that he hasn't come here and, uh,

131
07:35.686 --> 07:37.646
he misses Dad's dishes so much.

132
07:38.522 --> 07:42.025
And I just turned him away with the restaurant in this state.

133
07:43.026 --> 07:44.319
I'm so ashamed.

134
07:44.403 --> 07:46.738
[Du-yeong sighs] Song-yi.

135
07:46.822 --> 07:50.325
Go home and get some rest, okay? The kitchen is mostly cleaned up now.

136
07:50.409 --> 07:52.661
I'll check thoroughly tomorrow.

137
07:53.578 --> 07:55.664
[sighs] I'm sorry.

138
07:56.498 --> 07:57.749
This is all my fault.

139
08:00.210 --> 08:02.838
[sniffles, sighs]

140
08:02.921 --> 08:04.214
[sighs]

141
08:07.175 --> 08:08.552
[sighs]

142
08:11.221 --> 08:13.223
[sighing]

143
08:16.393 --> 08:18.353
[Song-yi crying]

144
08:23.900 --> 08:24.985
[sighs]

145
08:29.906 --> 08:32.659
[gentle music playing]

146
09:13.408 --> 09:14.785
You're still here, mister?

147
09:15.786 --> 09:16.870
[sighs]

148
09:16.953 --> 09:18.663
SPICY CHICKEN WITH DRIED PERSIMMON

149
09:18.747 --> 09:21.291
I'll clean up the rest tomorrow, so don't worry about it.

150
09:22.626 --> 09:23.710
[sighs]

151
09:23.794 --> 09:26.129
CHICKEN SO GOOD IT STOPS A CRYING CHILD

152
09:26.713 --> 09:28.298
Mister, please go now.

153
09:28.382 --> 09:31.301
Giving a dried persimmon to a crying child.

154
09:32.844 --> 09:36.264
Why would a crying child, even when told that a tiger would eat them,

155
09:36.932 --> 09:38.975
suddenly stop for a dried persimmon?

156
09:42.396 --> 09:43.397
That's…

157
09:47.317 --> 09:49.486
That's because the best cure for sadness…

158
09:54.032 --> 09:55.534
is none other than…

159
10:04.793 --> 10:06.920
well-prepared, delicious food.

160
10:07.712 --> 10:08.713
[chuckles]

161
10:12.884 --> 10:15.554
How long have you been cooking? What do you do?

162
10:16.430 --> 10:17.639
It's been one year.

163
10:18.265 --> 10:19.724
I'm still a commis.

164
10:19.808 --> 10:21.643
COMMIS: A JUNIOR-LEVEL KITCHEN STAFF

165
10:22.477 --> 10:26.106
By the way, what is it that you do exactly?

166
10:45.667 --> 10:46.918
We only have one guest,

167
10:47.002 --> 10:50.005
but she's the most important VIP you'll ever serve.

168
10:51.548 --> 10:53.633
Today's signature course consists

169
10:53.717 --> 10:55.969
of five dishes, from antipasto to dessert.

170
10:57.846 --> 10:59.723
I'd like you to serve the dinner tonight.

171
10:59.806 --> 11:02.017
Let's get it done within two hours, okay?

172
11:02.100 --> 11:03.101
Okay.

173
11:03.185 --> 11:04.394
[chuckles]

174
11:04.478 --> 11:06.855
All right, the antipasto first. Scallops.

175
11:06.938 --> 11:08.356
When searing scallops,

176
11:08.440 --> 11:12.152
wait until the pan is visibly billowing smoke before dropping them in.

177
11:12.235 --> 11:14.446
-Screaming hot, okay? -Okay.

178
11:15.197 --> 11:16.740
[Han] Sear each side for five seconds.

179
11:16.823 --> 11:19.451
SEARING: BROWNING THE OUTSIDE OVER HIGH HEAT

180
11:19.534 --> 11:22.454
That way, they're crisp on the outside with a juicy, medium center.

181
11:27.417 --> 11:30.420
These scallops are only about 80% fresh.

182
11:32.714 --> 11:34.925
We'll go with something other than the classic vongole sauce.

183
11:35.509 --> 11:37.886
The clams weren't purged right. They smelled.

184
11:39.012 --> 11:40.055
[grunts]

185
11:58.490 --> 12:01.701
Slice the ingredients, put them in a pot of oil

186
12:01.785 --> 12:03.286
and heat them slowly over low heat.

187
12:03.370 --> 12:05.372
"Slowly over a low heat."

188
12:08.041 --> 12:11.044
Leave it at medium for ten minutes, then…

189
12:11.127 --> 12:12.128
And then what?

190
12:13.421 --> 12:14.422
And then you blend it

191
12:14.506 --> 12:17.175
with brown rice vinegar and soy milk.

192
12:40.115 --> 12:41.616
Antipasto, scallops.

193
12:42.659 --> 12:45.495
ANTIPASTO - SEARED SCALLOPS WITH CHORIZO SAUCE

194
12:53.962 --> 12:54.963
[car lock beeps, clicks]

195
13:06.558 --> 13:07.726
[sighs]

196
13:13.189 --> 13:15.150
Huh? My phone.

197
13:17.110 --> 13:18.194
[gasps]

198
13:19.070 --> 13:20.530
[sighs]

199
13:22.991 --> 13:24.993
[magical music playing]

200
13:57.400 --> 13:58.860
[gasps]

201
13:58.943 --> 14:01.821
[emotional music playing]

202
14:02.864 --> 14:03.948
The sear

203
14:05.367 --> 14:06.368
is perfect.

204
14:09.245 --> 14:11.581
[Song-yi] The sear is perfect, but

205
14:11.665 --> 14:14.042
the scallops weren't as fresh as they should be.

206
14:14.918 --> 14:19.047
So he masked it with the chorizo sauce with a strong, meaty flavor.

207
14:19.130 --> 14:21.257
[Han] Primo piatti, ravioli.

208
14:21.341 --> 14:22.717
Ravioli!

209
14:24.552 --> 14:27.097
The shrimp in the ravioli seemed to be spoiled.

210
14:27.806 --> 14:29.140
How old were the shrimp?

211
14:29.224 --> 14:31.685
[sighs] Uh, three days?

212
14:36.773 --> 14:37.774
Five days.

213
14:37.857 --> 14:39.943
[sighs]

214
14:42.028 --> 14:43.154
A week old.

215
14:47.242 --> 14:48.243
What about the pasta?

216
14:48.326 --> 14:52.080
We normally use only fresh pasta, not dried pasta,

217
14:52.163 --> 14:55.959
but, you see, our chef de partie quit this afternoon.

218
14:58.044 --> 14:59.254
[sighs]

219
15:04.926 --> 15:05.927
[sighs]

220
15:06.010 --> 15:07.137
FISHCAKE

221
15:08.596 --> 15:09.639
EGGPLANT

222
15:14.936 --> 15:15.937
SUGAR

223
15:18.940 --> 15:21.234
For the primo, we'll make pasta instead of ravioli.

224
15:21.317 --> 15:23.737
Only, we'll make the noodles out of fishcake.

225
15:24.904 --> 15:26.156
Out of fishcake?

226
15:27.031 --> 15:29.075
First, let's make the tomato sauce.

227
16:08.698 --> 16:10.700
[upbeat music playing]

228
16:33.264 --> 16:35.892
EGGPLANT PASTA WITH FISHCAKE NOODLES

229
16:37.894 --> 16:40.271
Primo, tomato pasta. Go.

230
16:47.195 --> 16:50.782
I left my phone behind. Oh.

231
16:50.865 --> 16:53.243
The primo piatti is tomato…

232
16:54.285 --> 16:56.996
sauce pasta, ma'am. [breathes shakily]

233
16:58.790 --> 17:03.044
Didn't you say earlier that your kitchen was in no state to cook in tonight?

234
17:03.670 --> 17:06.548
Uh, well, you see… [chuckles]

235
17:10.134 --> 17:11.636
[chuckles]

236
17:21.104 --> 17:24.524
REVENUE MODEL THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026

237
17:29.696 --> 17:32.574
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026 SHOW CONCEPT

238
17:34.701 --> 17:36.995
THE WORLD'S BEST K-FOOD CHEF

239
17:39.163 --> 17:41.958
"The world's best K-food chef…"

240
17:57.015 --> 17:58.016
Hmm?

241
17:58.600 --> 17:59.976
What's this?

242
18:01.019 --> 18:02.812
I think it's fishcake.

243
18:03.938 --> 18:04.939
Fishcake?

244
18:15.408 --> 18:16.409
Mmm.

245
18:17.911 --> 18:18.912
Hmm?

246
18:26.878 --> 18:29.339
The risotto rice was dry and crumbly.

247
18:29.422 --> 18:32.383
Oh, it's probably because the rice is old.

248
18:32.967 --> 18:35.470
Our supplier stopped carrying arborio so

249
18:35.553 --> 18:37.764
we have been using cheap rice instead.

250
18:39.265 --> 18:41.935
Do you have other grains? Barley, anything like that?

251
18:42.018 --> 18:43.770
Yes, we do have barley.

252
18:44.395 --> 18:45.980
Oh, we have millet too.

253
18:57.659 --> 18:59.577
[sniffs, chuckles]

254
18:59.661 --> 19:00.662
Okay.

255
19:04.457 --> 19:06.417
[whirring]

256
19:27.105 --> 19:29.899
[Han] Barley and millet have a nice, springy bite.

257
19:29.983 --> 19:33.653
They'll definitely have more chew than a cheap rice risotto.

258
19:35.029 --> 19:36.614
To maximize that texture…

259
19:44.122 --> 19:45.915
Forget the spinach. Seafood.

260
19:45.999 --> 19:48.167
Uh, all we have are those scallops

261
19:48.251 --> 19:49.711
and a handful of smelly clams.

262
19:50.545 --> 19:52.714
I saw a market nearby on the way here.

263
19:52.797 --> 19:55.049
-Can we go there? -To the market?

264
19:55.133 --> 19:57.427
That's about a 20-minute trip.

265
19:57.510 --> 19:59.095
-Cuttlefish. -Sorry?

266
19:59.887 --> 20:01.764
Cuttlefish. In ten minutes.

267
20:02.473 --> 20:04.183
-Quick. Hurry. Let's go! -Uh--

268
20:05.059 --> 20:06.060
Wait.

269
20:06.811 --> 20:09.564
And a can of mixed nuts with a lot of macadamias.

270
20:10.606 --> 20:12.358
And a can of peaches.

271
20:12.442 --> 20:13.568
[chuckles]

272
20:13.651 --> 20:15.778
Please. I'm counting on you.

273
20:18.489 --> 20:19.490
-One more thing. -[gasps]

274
20:22.285 --> 20:23.786
There's an oil shop on the way.

275
20:24.704 --> 20:26.789
Get a freshly pressed bottle of pine nut oil.

276
20:27.331 --> 20:28.332
[sighs]

277
20:28.833 --> 20:29.917
Pine nut oil…

278
20:31.753 --> 20:34.005
-[door opens] -[chuckles]

279
20:37.508 --> 20:38.885
[tires squealing]

280
20:51.189 --> 20:52.857
[Han] The texture alone isn't enough.

281
20:53.566 --> 20:54.776
It needs aroma.

282
20:54.859 --> 20:56.027
Something powerful.

283
20:57.278 --> 20:58.488
What can I use?

284
21:25.973 --> 21:26.808
WALNUTS

285
21:26.891 --> 21:27.767
SARDINIAN PECORINO CHEESE

286
21:30.353 --> 21:31.896
[whirring]

287
21:45.451 --> 21:47.203
[motorcycle engine revving]

288
21:52.166 --> 21:53.251
[tires screech]

289
22:26.701 --> 22:28.369
[whirring]

290
22:46.762 --> 22:49.557
[Du-yeong] Why is he grinding all that by hand?

291
22:49.640 --> 22:52.977
Cooking tastes better when made by hand? Is that it?

292
22:54.562 --> 22:55.563
Chef?

293
23:01.194 --> 23:02.195
Bang.

294
23:03.404 --> 23:04.405
Bingo.

295
23:06.532 --> 23:07.617
[chuckles]

296
23:29.847 --> 23:31.641
CUTTLEFISH RISOTTO

297
23:39.565 --> 23:42.109
[gasps] Wow.

298
23:43.569 --> 23:45.404
Wow. What is this?

299
23:45.488 --> 23:46.530
[gasps]

300
23:46.614 --> 23:48.574
The rice and the cuttlefish

301
23:48.658 --> 23:50.409
both taste insane.

302
23:51.160 --> 23:52.203
Mmm.

303
23:53.746 --> 23:56.457
There's barley and something else in here too.

304
23:57.208 --> 23:58.209
[sniffs]

305
23:58.834 --> 24:00.878
What's giving it this unique aroma, Ms. Choi?

306
24:07.718 --> 24:09.136
[fork scrapes]

307
24:18.396 --> 24:20.273
[sizzling]

308
24:32.743 --> 24:33.869
[screams]

309
24:33.953 --> 24:35.162
[chuckles]

310
24:36.831 --> 24:37.832
Latex.

311
24:47.300 --> 24:48.426
[sighs]

312
25:00.396 --> 25:01.480
Wow.

313
25:02.481 --> 25:04.775
[sizzling]

314
25:18.456 --> 25:20.374
[Han] Burdock puree, squeeze bottle.

315
25:28.924 --> 25:31.260
Crown daisy pesto, small bottle.

316
26:22.228 --> 26:25.106
[Du-yeong] It looks done. Why isn't he telling me to serve it?

317
27:06.230 --> 27:07.523
Oh…

318
27:10.234 --> 27:12.528
[smoke hissing]

319
27:12.611 --> 27:18.033
BLACK GOAT STEAK IN PINE SMOKE

320
27:23.414 --> 27:24.790
[Jeong-won sighs]

321
27:25.541 --> 27:26.834
Huh…

322
27:27.418 --> 27:28.461
This is just…

323
27:30.463 --> 27:32.089
How should I put it?

324
27:32.173 --> 27:35.676
[Jeong-won] Every single dish is based on a classic Italian recipe,

325
27:35.759 --> 27:38.846
yet they've given them a such a modern and sophisticated touch.

326
27:38.929 --> 27:41.849
Huh. Famiglia is still delivering this caliber of food

327
27:41.932 --> 27:43.934
even without Chef Choi Seung-hyo?

328
27:45.936 --> 27:48.689
[sighs] Excuse me. I need the restroom.

329
27:48.772 --> 27:49.773
Oh, of course.

330
28:07.208 --> 28:09.251
[mysterious music playing]

331
28:19.261 --> 28:20.596
[shutter clicking]

332
28:25.726 --> 28:26.727
CHEF CHA

333
28:29.855 --> 28:30.856
Hey, Woo-jin.

334
28:32.733 --> 28:33.734
So, uh…

335
28:34.276 --> 28:35.277
[inhales]

336
28:36.278 --> 28:37.655
It's a long story.

337
28:38.364 --> 28:40.199
Can I explain it to you later?

338
28:50.584 --> 28:51.585
[phone beeps]

339
29:00.386 --> 29:03.180
ORDER FOR TABLE 3

340
29:08.644 --> 29:11.397
Table three's order, how long do we have left until it's complete?

341
29:11.480 --> 29:12.731
Two minutes, Chef.

342
29:12.815 --> 29:15.734
Table eight still hasn't gotten their mains. Where are their quails?

343
29:15.818 --> 29:18.279
They're done. We'll garnish them and send them out right away.

344
29:18.362 --> 29:19.405
Everyone, move it!

345
29:19.488 --> 29:20.364
[claps]

346
29:20.447 --> 29:23.158
We're running behind. We got two complaints already.

347
29:23.242 --> 29:24.493
[all] Yes, Chef!

348
29:36.880 --> 29:39.300
[Jeong-won] It's not like I haven't tasted those dishes before.

349
29:40.092 --> 29:43.137
And yet, they all tasted completely new to me.

350
30:02.114 --> 30:03.157
Excuse me.

351
30:03.907 --> 30:06.994
Are you the chef who prepared the food that was served to me tonight?

352
30:08.746 --> 30:09.747
Yes, that's right.

353
30:10.623 --> 30:13.709
I heard Famiglia's head chef position was vacant.

354
30:14.585 --> 30:16.086
Are you the new head chef?

355
30:16.879 --> 30:17.963
[chuckles]

356
30:18.047 --> 30:19.214
Well, no.

357
30:19.298 --> 30:21.634
I just happened to cook here for tonight.

358
30:22.301 --> 30:23.302
Oh, then,

359
30:23.844 --> 30:27.181
may I ask which restaurant you work at when you're not here?

360
30:28.432 --> 30:29.433
Uh…

361
30:30.809 --> 30:34.355
I'm just someone who happened to stop by.

362
30:37.566 --> 30:38.651
Goodbye.

363
30:39.610 --> 30:40.653
Your cooking tonight…

364
30:45.449 --> 30:46.950
it was really impressive.

365
30:47.701 --> 30:50.079
I had to find out who put this together.

366
30:50.162 --> 30:51.747
Sorry if I was prying too much.

367
31:06.053 --> 31:07.221
[sighs]

368
31:07.304 --> 31:08.305
[Song-yi] Oh, you're going?

369
31:08.389 --> 31:09.807
They just served dessert.

370
31:09.890 --> 31:11.225
I'm sorry, Ms. Choi.

371
31:11.308 --> 31:12.935
I really have to get going.

372
31:13.018 --> 31:15.104
Oh, well, all right.

373
31:15.187 --> 31:17.439
Ms. Choi, thank you for the meal.

374
31:17.523 --> 31:19.358
I really enjoyed it.

375
31:19.441 --> 31:21.527
Uh, I'll have the dessert next time.

376
31:24.446 --> 31:26.198
Excuse me. Just a moment.

377
31:31.203 --> 31:32.830
Oh, you really didn't have to.

378
31:34.206 --> 31:35.207
[sighs]

379
31:36.959 --> 31:39.044
The kitchen staff put a lot of work into it,

380
31:39.128 --> 31:40.713
so it would be a shame if you didn't try it.

381
31:40.796 --> 31:43.799
If you plan on eating it tomorrow, please make sure to keep it in the fridge.

382
31:45.676 --> 31:46.802
Thank you.

383
31:48.178 --> 31:50.097
-See you again, Ms. Choi. -Sure.

384
31:58.021 --> 31:59.106
[sighs]

385
32:00.983 --> 32:02.985
Hey, sorry for waking you.

386
32:03.068 --> 32:05.446
It's dawn over there. I called too early, didn't I?

387
32:05.529 --> 32:08.615
[sighs] I know. That's how urgent this is.

388
32:08.699 --> 32:10.826
I sent you a few photos a little while ago.

389
32:10.909 --> 32:13.912
[inhales] Well, I think he's a chef.

390
32:13.996 --> 32:15.831
Find out who he is and do it fast.

391
32:18.000 --> 32:20.043
I don't know. I've never seen him before.

392
32:20.127 --> 32:22.004
I'll explain the details later.

393
32:22.087 --> 32:25.591
Just send the photos around to a few people you trust and find out who he is.

394
32:26.091 --> 32:28.719
[chuckles] Okay. Call me right back.

395
32:30.179 --> 32:31.263
[call ends]

396
32:32.639 --> 32:33.932
[earbud clatters]

397
32:41.523 --> 32:44.109
[grunting] Goodness. [groaning]

398
32:44.943 --> 32:46.653
Oh, goodness, my back.

399
32:47.279 --> 32:48.739
[grunting]

400
33:01.960 --> 33:03.587
[exhales]

401
33:17.267 --> 33:19.311
I'm not sure if the food was to your liking.

402
33:19.812 --> 33:22.731
I did my best, but we were short on ingredients.

403
33:22.815 --> 33:24.983
Oh, no. It was so…

404
33:25.067 --> 33:26.819
It was so delicious.

405
33:26.902 --> 33:28.362
I barely had time to think.

406
33:29.863 --> 33:30.864
I'm really glad.

407
33:30.948 --> 33:32.741
Thank you so very much.

408
33:33.492 --> 33:37.329
I could feel the heart and sincerity you put into the food.

409
33:38.205 --> 33:40.082
You really impressed me.

410
33:40.165 --> 33:41.708
It felt just like my dad's cooking.

411
33:42.876 --> 33:44.878
[gentle music playing]

412
33:46.588 --> 33:47.840
I'm sorry about earlier.

413
33:49.174 --> 33:51.176
I didn't know the full story.

414
33:55.055 --> 33:57.391
I didn't know Chef Choi Seung-hyo had passed away.

415
33:59.393 --> 34:00.644
Yeah.

416
34:06.525 --> 34:08.360
I'm really sorry for your loss.

417
34:12.531 --> 34:13.657
It's okay, thanks.

418
34:21.748 --> 34:23.041
-[door opens] -Oh, wait.

419
34:24.793 --> 34:27.379
I haven't even thanked you properly for tonight.

420
34:27.462 --> 34:30.382
At least, tell me what your name is or an address of where you--

421
34:30.465 --> 34:31.842
Oh, don't worry about it.

422
34:31.925 --> 34:34.011
I'm leaving for New York tomorrow.

423
34:34.553 --> 34:35.554
What?

424
34:35.637 --> 34:37.890
You take care now, okay?

425
34:42.686 --> 34:44.313
[door closes]

426
34:44.396 --> 34:45.397
Hmm.

427
34:49.818 --> 34:51.320
[Woo-jin] Great work, everyone.

428
34:52.529 --> 34:56.867
We had a few demanding VIP tables tonight. It must've been tougher than usual.

429
34:56.950 --> 35:00.454
But still, you made it through to the end without any major mistakes.

430
35:00.537 --> 35:01.997
Great work to everyone here.

431
35:03.707 --> 35:05.626
Especially Michael.

432
35:05.709 --> 35:06.919
Yes, Chef.

433
35:07.002 --> 35:09.504
We got a lot of complaints on the main dish tonight.

434
35:10.005 --> 35:12.925
Sweetbread isn't easy to cook properly.

435
35:13.008 --> 35:14.301
Nice work.

436
35:14.885 --> 35:15.886
Thank you so much, Chef.

437
35:15.969 --> 35:17.846
-Check the temperatures in the aging room. -Of course…

438
35:17.930 --> 35:19.973
-…and storage cooler one more time. -…their ingredients are top notch.

439
35:20.057 --> 35:22.392
Just make sure you haven't missed anything. That's it for today.

440
35:22.976 --> 35:24.186
[all] Great work today, Chef.

441
35:27.189 --> 35:29.566
All right. You all did well today.

442
35:30.484 --> 35:31.568
My throat's a little scratchy,

443
35:31.652 --> 35:34.363
so how about some pork belly and soju to wash it all down?

444
35:34.446 --> 35:37.032
[cheering]

445
35:37.115 --> 35:40.786
Don't drink too much, though. Tomorrow's customers won't be easy.

446
35:40.869 --> 35:42.704
-[all] Yes, Chef! -Wrap it up!

447
35:42.788 --> 35:45.624
[cheering]

448
35:48.919 --> 35:50.921
[gentle music playing]

449
36:00.430 --> 36:02.015
[sighs]

450
36:34.172 --> 36:35.549
Hey, hey.

451
36:35.632 --> 36:38.385
I'd heard about this place, but seeing it in person…

452
36:38.468 --> 36:41.680
Wow, your restaurant's really something. [laughing]

453
36:41.763 --> 36:42.764
Yeah.

454
36:43.765 --> 36:45.308
Looking good, Cha Woo-jin.

455
36:46.351 --> 36:50.188
[chuckling] Business must be good. You're practically glowing, yeah?

456
36:50.272 --> 36:51.440
Okay, then. How much?

457
36:51.523 --> 36:52.691
Huh?

458
36:52.774 --> 36:54.234
How much more

459
36:55.444 --> 36:57.029
do you need…

460
36:58.321 --> 36:59.906
that you came all the way over here?

461
37:01.199 --> 37:03.118
[sighing] Come on now.

462
37:04.494 --> 37:06.079
You're really as impatient as ever.

463
37:06.788 --> 37:07.789
Listen.

464
37:09.207 --> 37:12.127
There's a proper order to things and a proper flow to a conversation.

465
37:12.210 --> 37:14.337
How many tables do you think I serve?

466
37:14.421 --> 37:17.924
I don't know… Maybe 12, 13, I guess?

467
37:18.008 --> 37:19.468
We have exactly 15.

468
37:21.011 --> 37:22.345
Each table seats,

469
37:22.971 --> 37:25.307
on a normal day, two to four people.

470
37:27.184 --> 37:30.020
For dinner alone, we have our first seating at 6:00

471
37:30.645 --> 37:32.814
and our second seating is at 8:00.

472
37:33.607 --> 37:35.067
Tonight, we were fully booked.

473
37:35.150 --> 37:38.195
Even at only four guests per table, that's 60 per seating.

474
37:38.278 --> 37:39.946
120 total.

475
37:40.030 --> 37:43.116
Twenty front-of-house staff and 15 in the kitchen

476
37:43.200 --> 37:44.534
have to move at a breakneck pace

477
37:44.618 --> 37:46.578
to deliver the absolute best food and service

478
37:46.661 --> 37:48.663
to nearly ten times that number of guests,

479
37:48.747 --> 37:50.457
whether we burn our arms,

480
37:51.500 --> 37:54.836
cut our fingers on sharp knives, sprain an ankle or…

481
37:55.879 --> 37:57.547
end up with a cast.

482
37:57.631 --> 37:59.007
Why?

483
37:59.091 --> 38:01.093
Because once a customer is disappointed…

484
38:02.761 --> 38:04.137
they never come back.

485
38:08.683 --> 38:09.684
You see…

486
38:12.687 --> 38:16.066
it might look like we're just whipping up food on the fly here,

487
38:16.149 --> 38:20.153
but every single second I'm stuck bickering with you is precious time I need

488
38:20.695 --> 38:23.657
to prepare providing the best service possible.

489
38:23.740 --> 38:26.827
You think I have time to waste on some neighborhood thug like you?

490
38:29.246 --> 38:30.247
No, I don't.

491
38:32.165 --> 38:34.459
So stop wasting my time and spill it.

492
38:35.502 --> 38:36.503
That woman…

493
38:38.964 --> 38:41.424
How much did she tell you to collect this time?

494
38:45.178 --> 38:46.638
[Hyung-gi sighs]

495
38:50.767 --> 38:51.768
[inhales sharply]

496
38:52.811 --> 38:54.271
Don't you worry too much.

497
38:54.354 --> 38:57.315
She only needs to stay in the hospital for about ten days.

498
38:57.399 --> 38:59.317
You see, at your mom's age,

499
38:59.401 --> 39:01.611
hip injuries like this are fairly common.

500
39:01.695 --> 39:05.490
At least she doesn't need surgery. That's a relief, isn't it? Huh?

501
39:05.574 --> 39:09.035
[chuckles] Anyway, thanks so much.

502
39:10.203 --> 39:13.248
You've really put my mind at ease.

503
39:13.331 --> 39:16.918
Oh, and, uh, I'll tell your mom to give you a call when she's out.

504
39:17.961 --> 39:19.921
You didn't say which hospital that she's in.

505
39:22.883 --> 39:24.759
-[zipper closes] -What?

506
39:27.679 --> 39:29.556
Are you afraid I might go visit?

507
39:31.099 --> 39:32.267
[chuckles]

508
39:35.604 --> 39:36.980
You know something, kid?

509
39:37.689 --> 39:39.149
You haven't changed a bit.

510
39:40.233 --> 39:41.735
[sighs]

511
39:41.818 --> 39:43.987
Killing your own father is something else.

512
39:45.363 --> 39:47.824
[somber music plays]

513
39:50.952 --> 39:52.120
Whoa.

514
39:52.871 --> 39:54.873
You look like you're gonna shoot lasers.

515
39:56.082 --> 40:00.045
With that scary look, who would dare to talk to you? Huh?

516
40:07.594 --> 40:08.595
Anyway, thanks.

517
40:24.527 --> 40:26.363
CHAIRWOMAN MOON HAE-SEON

518
40:26.446 --> 40:28.490
[phone buzzing]

519
40:33.286 --> 40:34.287
Yes, Chairwoman.

520
40:34.371 --> 40:36.539
Are you still at the restaurant?

521
40:37.540 --> 40:40.043
[Woo-jin] Ah, yes. I'm just wrapping up.

522
40:41.211 --> 40:44.005
[sighs] I see. You're working awfully late.

523
40:44.089 --> 40:45.090
[chuckles]

524
40:46.132 --> 40:49.427
I heard Ms. Seon couldn't take Mr. Bernier there today.

525
40:50.178 --> 40:53.390
Oh, yes. It seems that something came up.

526
40:54.057 --> 40:55.183
He's an important guest,

527
40:55.267 --> 40:57.936
so I wanted to book a table for him at your place.

528
40:59.312 --> 41:02.774
Ms. Seon has been working very diligently for the company.

529
41:03.608 --> 41:08.280
No one is saying it, but everyone's on high alert right now.

530
41:09.781 --> 41:10.782
Right.

531
41:11.574 --> 41:13.952
Could you free up a table for tomorrow evening?

532
41:14.035 --> 41:17.539
I think I'll escort Mr. Bernier myself. But if you can't, that's okay.

533
41:17.622 --> 41:20.000
No, it's fine.

534
41:20.083 --> 41:21.710
I'll free up a table for you.

535
41:23.920 --> 41:26.423
But why do you sound so down right now?

536
41:26.506 --> 41:28.174
Are you sick or something?

537
41:29.426 --> 41:30.427
No, I'm fine.

538
41:31.928 --> 41:33.722
We just had a lot of customers today.

539
41:33.805 --> 41:36.308
I'm tired, that's all.

540
41:39.519 --> 41:42.063
I'll send you a month's worth of herbal tonic this weekend.

541
41:42.147 --> 41:43.231
Make sure you take it.

542
41:43.315 --> 41:45.817
I'll tell Hwang to leave it at your apartment's management office.

543
41:46.443 --> 41:50.155
Oh, I still have some left from last time.

544
41:50.238 --> 41:53.533
Why do you still have some left? I told you to take it every day.

545
41:54.993 --> 41:56.244
I'm sorry. [chuckles]

546
41:56.911 --> 41:58.830
Make sure you drink one every day.

547
41:59.372 --> 42:02.208
You need to take even better care of yourself when you live alone.

548
42:02.292 --> 42:03.585
Right.

549
42:03.668 --> 42:05.462
I'm sorry to cause you concern.

550
42:05.545 --> 42:07.464
Okay. See you tomorrow.

551
42:07.547 --> 42:08.631
Bye-bye.

552
42:09.215 --> 42:11.468
Yes, Chairwoman. Good night.

553
42:12.427 --> 42:13.428
[phone beeps]

554
42:20.352 --> 42:23.480
[humming]

555
42:23.563 --> 42:25.273
[door unlocks]

556
42:25.357 --> 42:27.817
[humming continues]

557
42:34.282 --> 42:37.035
You're home. [sighs]

558
42:38.286 --> 42:40.121
Why are you so late?

559
42:40.205 --> 42:41.331
[groans]

560
42:43.458 --> 42:44.876
Why am I so late?

561
42:45.418 --> 42:46.419
Geez.

562
42:47.504 --> 42:50.507
I was working myself to the bone, that's why. Okay?

563
42:50.590 --> 42:54.219
Your husband's out there busting his ass… [sighs] …to make every penny he can.

564
42:54.302 --> 42:56.262
But here you are sleeping,

565
42:57.138 --> 42:58.473
without a care in the world.

566
42:59.599 --> 43:01.267
[sighs] What is it now?

567
43:01.851 --> 43:02.852
[gasps]

568
43:03.937 --> 43:05.230
Have you been drinking?

569
43:06.648 --> 43:07.774
With what money?

570
43:09.067 --> 43:12.487
Hey, whether I drink with the money I earned, or the money I begged for,

571
43:12.570 --> 43:14.864
it's not like you did anything to help, is it?

572
43:14.948 --> 43:16.366
-[clicks tongue] -[sighs]

573
43:16.449 --> 43:19.452
Don't tell me you… [breathes shakily] …went to see him again?

574
43:20.537 --> 43:22.163
-[sad music playing] -[breathing shakily]

575
43:22.247 --> 43:24.249
You didn't, did you?

576
43:24.332 --> 43:25.959
Did you go to his workplace again?

577
43:26.042 --> 43:28.128
[scoffs] What's it to you?

578
43:28.211 --> 43:30.964
[inhales sharply] Did you go there to ask him for money? Huh?

579
43:31.047 --> 43:34.843
Were you drinking and gambling all night with the money you took from him?

580
43:34.926 --> 43:36.553
-Enough, woman! -[grunts]

581
43:36.636 --> 43:40.723
How dare you interrogate me? Who are you, a cop? A detective? Huh?

582
43:41.933 --> 43:45.770
You promised you'd never go back to see him again. [breathing shakily]

583
43:45.854 --> 43:48.565
You said that would be the last time. [groans]

584
43:48.648 --> 43:49.941
Didn't you?

585
43:50.024 --> 43:52.527
-Why do you keep bothering him, huh? -[groaning]

586
43:52.610 --> 43:54.779
-You promised to leave him alone! -[strains]

587
43:54.863 --> 43:56.322
He's finally living a good life!

588
43:56.406 --> 43:57.490
-[shouting] Why? -[yells]

589
43:57.574 --> 44:00.076
-Why do you keep bothering him? Why? -Hey! Who'd you think you're…

590
44:00.160 --> 44:01.161
W-Why, let go of me!

591
44:01.244 --> 44:03.913
Do you still think you're a cop? [breathes shakily]

592
44:03.997 --> 44:06.416
You got kicked out for extorting money.

593
44:07.167 --> 44:08.626
Aren't you ashamed of yourself?

594
44:09.836 --> 44:11.546
Who the hell do you think you're talking to?

595
44:11.629 --> 44:13.047
-Do you have a death wish, huh? -[gasps, chokes]

596
44:13.131 --> 44:15.800
-Come here. -[gasps, groans]

597
44:15.884 --> 44:18.011
[gasps, groans]

598
44:18.094 --> 44:19.888
Know your place.

599
44:19.971 --> 44:23.224
-You've got some nerve. -[groaning]

600
44:23.308 --> 44:26.769
I-I was wrong. No, please…

601
44:26.853 --> 44:28.771
[screams] Please, honey!

602
44:28.855 --> 44:29.939
Damn it!

603
44:38.865 --> 44:40.074
[groans]

604
44:40.617 --> 44:42.660
[sobs, breathes shakily]

605
44:42.744 --> 44:44.496
[door opens]

606
44:44.579 --> 44:45.580
[sobs]

607
44:46.623 --> 44:47.749
[door slams]

608
44:50.543 --> 44:51.628
[sobs]

609
44:58.301 --> 45:00.720
[melancholy music plays]

610
45:07.519 --> 45:08.520
[groans]

611
45:10.271 --> 45:12.982
[crying]

612
45:16.986 --> 45:18.488
[quiet clattering]

613
45:40.385 --> 45:42.220
Oh. Chef.

614
45:42.804 --> 45:45.265
-You're still here? -Yes, Chef.

615
45:46.015 --> 45:48.893
-Go eat. -Oh. [chuckles]

616
45:48.977 --> 45:51.104
I had a few things to finish up.

617
45:55.066 --> 45:56.109
What are you making?

618
45:56.192 --> 45:57.443
Yes, it's beurre blanc.

619
45:58.069 --> 46:00.321
I tried adding a Korean citrusy element to it.

620
46:00.405 --> 46:01.531
Like what?

621
46:01.614 --> 46:02.824
Persimmon vinegar.

622
46:03.992 --> 46:05.451
Oh, and toward the end,

623
46:05.535 --> 46:08.871
I tried adding angelica leaves instead of the usual herbs.

624
46:14.127 --> 46:16.796
It goes pretty well with Korean freshwater fish,

625
46:16.879 --> 46:19.173
so I gave it a try.

626
46:34.105 --> 46:35.106
Bae Yeong-su.

627
46:35.189 --> 46:36.190
Yes, Chef.

628
46:37.942 --> 46:39.068
How long has it been…

629
46:41.195 --> 46:42.405
since you joined Exception?

630
46:42.488 --> 46:44.157
Oh.

631
46:44.240 --> 46:45.241
Uh…

632
46:45.325 --> 46:47.452
It'll be three years in two months, Chef.

633
46:49.370 --> 46:51.914
Next month, you're in charge of the fish station.

634
46:51.998 --> 46:53.291
Sorry?

635
46:54.709 --> 46:56.336
You've worked here long enough.

636
46:58.046 --> 46:58.963
[stammers]

637
46:59.047 --> 47:01.758
Oh, y-yes. Okay, Chef.

638
47:03.301 --> 47:04.636
Keep it to yourself for now.

639
47:05.303 --> 47:06.596
Yes, understood, Chef.

640
47:08.014 --> 47:10.808
Oh, uh… [clears throat] I'll do my best, Chef.

641
47:10.892 --> 47:11.893
Thank you.

642
47:20.109 --> 47:24.280
So he never takes the head chef position and only ever works as sous-chef?

643
47:24.364 --> 47:26.908
[scoffs] Is that eccentric or just bizarre?

644
47:26.991 --> 47:28.618
[friend, on phone] It's both.

645
47:28.701 --> 47:32.163
But his style is too universal to call eccentric,

646
47:32.246 --> 47:34.332
and too brilliant to call bizarre.

647
47:34.415 --> 47:36.125
[Jeong-won] "Breaking down the border."

648
47:36.209 --> 47:39.003
"The chef of our time who breaks barriers.

649
47:39.087 --> 47:40.213
Chris K."

650
47:40.296 --> 47:41.506
[chuckles]

651
47:41.589 --> 47:43.049
It's a great headline.

652
47:43.132 --> 47:46.469
He's not a public person, so there aren't many photos of him.

653
47:47.387 --> 47:51.849
Anyway, you got to eat his food in Korea? I'm so jealous.

654
47:51.933 --> 47:53.267
Even here in New York,

655
47:53.351 --> 47:56.771
his restaurant is impossible to book less than six months in advance.

656
47:56.854 --> 47:57.855
TEAM AURELIA TAKES FIRST PLACE

657
47:57.939 --> 48:01.192
And since he went abroad, it's impossible to taste his food now.

658
48:01.275 --> 48:02.527
So how was it?

659
48:02.610 --> 48:05.863
Well… it's kinda hard to put into words.

660
48:06.698 --> 48:09.492
His style is definitely overwhelming,

661
48:09.575 --> 48:12.036
but it somehow feels familiar.

662
48:12.120 --> 48:14.747
It's a bit like something your mom would cook.

663
48:14.831 --> 48:16.374
[sighs] I don't know. [inhales sharply]

664
48:16.457 --> 48:18.835
I've never experienced this before.

665
48:24.382 --> 48:25.383
Hold on.

666
48:30.722 --> 48:34.058
Cha Woo-jin came… in second?

667
48:35.685 --> 48:37.812
A few years ago, was it?

668
48:37.895 --> 48:41.733
The team representing his restaurant won a cooking competition in Belgium,

669
48:41.816 --> 48:45.445
and the gap between the first and the second was so huge

670
48:45.528 --> 48:47.155
it caused quite a stir at the time.

671
48:47.238 --> 48:50.867
[chuckles] What's funny is, the winning recipe wasn't the head chef's,

672
48:50.950 --> 48:53.369
it was Chris K.'s, the sous-chef.

673
48:53.453 --> 48:56.038
So the reporters practically ignored the head chef

674
48:56.122 --> 48:58.958
and flocked to Chris K. to talk to him instead.

675
49:02.628 --> 49:04.714
SEON JEONG-WON PRODUCTION TEAM ONE

676
49:17.101 --> 49:18.227
So you're…

677
49:19.145 --> 49:21.147
looking for the best Korean chef there is?

678
49:26.027 --> 49:29.071
I don't get it. What exactly does Pyeongyeon want with us?

679
49:35.578 --> 49:36.579
[sips]

680
49:40.333 --> 49:41.751
Obviously,

681
49:42.877 --> 49:45.254
to ask Famiglia to take part in the competition.

682
49:46.547 --> 49:50.927
I know exactly how you feel about Pyeongyeon Group, Ms. Choi.

683
49:51.761 --> 49:54.639
I know no words could ever comfort you… [inhales sharply]

684
49:57.809 --> 50:00.186
And that nothing we do will clear up the squabble.

685
50:00.269 --> 50:01.646
[gasps]

686
50:01.729 --> 50:03.147
[shakily] Squabble?

687
50:03.231 --> 50:05.066
Did you just call it a squabble?

688
50:06.359 --> 50:07.527
[scoffs]

689
50:07.610 --> 50:09.362
[sad music playing]

690
50:09.987 --> 50:11.364
[Song-yi sniffles]

691
50:12.073 --> 50:13.157
[scoffs]

692
50:13.241 --> 50:14.909
THE TABLE: K-CHEF 2026

693
50:16.244 --> 50:17.245
[sniffles]

694
50:19.330 --> 50:20.331
I know…

695
50:22.333 --> 50:24.502
why you people are holding this competition.

696
50:26.128 --> 50:28.673
This isn't about getting rid of Plate In Asia.

697
50:29.715 --> 50:33.219
You're just trying to erase us. Erase Famiglia, and my dad too.

698
50:35.263 --> 50:37.640
[sighs] And all of your own wrongdoings.

699
50:40.935 --> 50:42.812
[sighs]

700
50:44.438 --> 50:48.359
Once this competition is over, people will completely forget Famiglia.

701
50:49.402 --> 50:52.530
And my father, who died unjustly fighting Pyeongyeon.

702
50:53.489 --> 50:54.490
Isn't that right?

703
50:56.284 --> 51:00.079
And the winner of this competition will just end up hogging the spotlight.

704
51:00.162 --> 51:03.165
Their restaurant will have people lining up every single day starting from day one.

705
51:03.249 --> 51:04.959
Their life story will go viral, they'll be on TV,

706
51:05.042 --> 51:06.252
not to mention the commercials.

707
51:08.212 --> 51:12.174
Pyeongyeon will keep using them to create one business opportunity after another.

708
51:13.509 --> 51:17.805
And with that puppet of theirs, Pyeongyeon Group will… [inhales sharply]

709
51:17.889 --> 51:21.642
…divert everyone's attention, and, like they always have…

710
51:21.726 --> 51:24.103
[breathes shakily] …Pyeongyeon will remain on top.

711
51:31.944 --> 51:33.154
Ms. Choi Song-yi.

712
51:40.161 --> 51:42.413
[inhales sharply, sighs]

713
51:43.873 --> 51:46.792
I've been planning this competition for five years

714
51:46.876 --> 51:50.713
with the sole belief that Korean food can stand at the heart of the world's cuisine.

715
51:51.797 --> 51:54.133
This corporate agenda that you think I have?

716
51:56.344 --> 51:59.096
I'm not sacrificing this competition for an agenda.

717
52:00.097 --> 52:01.140
I assure you.

718
52:02.308 --> 52:03.517
[sighs] Please.

719
52:03.601 --> 52:05.645
Think about it one more time.

720
52:05.728 --> 52:08.606
Have Famiglia… join the competition.

721
52:12.026 --> 52:14.153
Sure. I understand.

722
52:15.321 --> 52:17.031
I appreciate the offer…

723
52:18.866 --> 52:21.118
but do you really think we could even enter?

724
52:24.789 --> 52:26.290
Just look at our restaurant.

725
52:28.042 --> 52:30.002
We don't even have a head chef.

726
52:33.005 --> 52:34.131
You do have one.

727
52:35.007 --> 52:36.008
Who?

728
52:36.634 --> 52:39.595
That man who cooked that incredible food yesterday.

729
52:41.305 --> 52:45.601
The hottest Korean chef on the global scene right now.

730
52:47.478 --> 52:48.521
Chris K.

731
52:53.818 --> 52:56.112
[Jeong-won] What is it that you really want?

732
52:57.071 --> 52:59.323
To win a lawsuit against Pyeongyeon Group?

733
53:01.575 --> 53:05.287
Isn't your father's name and honor

734
53:05.371 --> 53:08.290
and Famiglia's reputation more important than that?

735
53:12.169 --> 53:14.338
No one knows how long the lawsuit will take.

736
53:14.422 --> 53:17.049
And going up against Pyeongyeon will cost you a fortune.

737
53:17.133 --> 53:19.468
The longer it drags on,

738
53:19.552 --> 53:21.512
the more people will forget about

739
53:21.595 --> 53:24.348
Chef Choi Seung-hyo and Famiglia alike.

740
53:29.270 --> 53:31.313
[Jeong-won] Win this competition.

741
53:31.397 --> 53:34.608
Then you'll be able to restore your father and Famiglia's name,

742
53:35.443 --> 53:38.446
and people will pay more attention to what you have to say.

743
53:38.529 --> 53:42.366
Winning the competition is the only way for you to save Famiglia. Listen to me.

744
53:43.492 --> 53:44.869
You need to get Chris K.

745
53:46.454 --> 53:50.124
Then you can save Famiglia and restore your father's name and honor.

746
53:52.585 --> 53:54.253
Then you can go after the lawsuit.

747
53:56.881 --> 53:57.882
I'm…

748
53:59.800 --> 54:02.344
offering you a deal right now, Ms. Choi Song-yi.

749
54:04.805 --> 54:07.016
A deal that stakes both Pyeongyeon Group…

750
54:10.311 --> 54:11.312
and Famiglia.

751
54:12.897 --> 54:15.107
[emotional music playing]

752
54:22.114 --> 54:23.616
TIME PULLS US APART

753
54:30.456 --> 54:32.833
[emotional music continues]

754
54:37.588 --> 54:39.090
SAN AIRLINES ICN TO JFK

755
54:55.773 --> 54:57.399
[approaching footsteps]

756
54:57.483 --> 54:59.485
[Song-yi] Excuse me! [pants]

757
54:59.568 --> 55:03.364
[panting]

758
55:05.533 --> 55:06.534
You're from Famiglia.

759
55:06.617 --> 55:08.369
[breathes heavily]

760
55:08.452 --> 55:11.413
[chuckles] Well, what are you doing here?

761
55:11.497 --> 55:13.249
Oh.

762
55:13.332 --> 55:18.170
Um, I was… all over the place yesterday that I didn't get to thank you properly.

763
55:18.254 --> 55:19.338
-[pants] -[chuckles]

764
55:19.421 --> 55:21.215
-What? -Uh…

765
55:21.298 --> 55:23.968
I thought… I heard you were leaving for New York today,

766
55:24.051 --> 55:25.553
so I came here to see…

767
55:26.428 --> 55:27.972
[sighs]

768
55:30.182 --> 55:31.433
Please help me.

769
55:39.024 --> 55:40.693
The best K-chef, huh?

770
55:41.485 --> 55:44.613
[chuckles] I understand your situation, but I can't do it.

771
55:46.824 --> 55:49.326
I'm starting at a new place the day after tomorrow.

772
55:50.911 --> 55:52.830
So, if I don't leave today,

773
55:52.913 --> 55:55.749
I'll be in breach of contract and have to pay a huge fine.

774
55:58.878 --> 55:59.837
[chuckles]

775
56:04.592 --> 56:05.926
[sighs]

776
56:06.594 --> 56:08.220
Even if I enter the competition,

777
56:09.221 --> 56:10.848
there's no guarantee I'll win.

778
56:11.432 --> 56:13.893
Besides, I'm not someone who can represent Famiglia.

779
56:14.935 --> 56:17.813
There's no time to prepare, or even a team…

780
56:19.690 --> 56:22.526
Well, anyway, it's just not possible for me.

781
56:24.904 --> 56:27.239
Let's go. I have a plane to catch.

782
56:34.705 --> 56:35.706
[sighs]

783
56:37.875 --> 56:39.877
Pyeongyeon Group killed my father!

784
56:39.960 --> 56:41.503
[sad music playing]

785
56:41.587 --> 56:44.256
Pyeongyeon Group was responsible for my father's death.

786
56:44.340 --> 56:47.927
They fabricated a bunch of lies and drove him to take his own life.

787
56:53.015 --> 56:54.892
I know why

788
56:54.975 --> 56:57.603
they're trying to hold this competition now.

789
56:58.479 --> 57:01.023
They're trying to bury the truth about my father's death.

790
57:01.649 --> 57:04.485
They'll make sure the puppet they put forward wins the competition.

791
57:04.568 --> 57:06.737
That's what Pyeongyeon has always done.

792
57:06.820 --> 57:09.448
They get rid of anyone who doesn't suit their tastes

793
57:09.531 --> 57:12.868
and they fill their ranks with people who take their side without question.

794
57:14.453 --> 57:15.829
Please help me.

795
57:17.748 --> 57:21.585
I want to show them just once, even if it's just this once,

796
57:21.669 --> 57:24.588
that they can't always have their way.

797
57:26.382 --> 57:29.176
I want to prove it to my late father.

798
57:29.885 --> 57:32.930
I want to prove it to the people who killed him.

799
57:35.266 --> 57:36.809
[Song-yi] Pyeongyeon killed my father.

800
57:36.892 --> 57:38.936
[teenage Han] Pyeongyeon killed my dad.

801
57:44.942 --> 57:47.027
[breathes shakily]

802
57:47.945 --> 57:49.238
Pyeongyeon killed my dad.

803
57:49.321 --> 57:51.991
I said, Pyeongyeon killed my dad!

804
57:52.074 --> 57:55.786
[breathing heavily]

805
58:20.978 --> 58:22.855
[gasping]

806
58:24.940 --> 58:26.191
[gasps]

807
58:26.275 --> 58:27.359
[grunts]

808
58:29.069 --> 58:32.031
-[grunting] -[banging on door]

809
58:32.114 --> 58:36.744
-Open the door! -[dog barking]

810
58:36.827 --> 58:38.704
[groaning, panting]

811
58:38.787 --> 58:41.790
[dog barking continues]

812
58:44.543 --> 58:45.669
[grunts]

813
58:46.754 --> 58:49.173
[young Han sobs] Dad!

814
58:50.382 --> 58:51.550
Dad, please!

815
58:51.633 --> 58:53.052
Open your eyes, Han!

816
58:53.135 --> 58:55.637
Wake up, Han. Kang Han!

817
58:56.764 --> 58:57.806
[gasps]

818
59:02.061 --> 59:03.062
Hey!

819
59:03.145 --> 59:06.023
-You don't belong here. -Go to your country. Leave!

820
59:06.106 --> 59:07.107
[panting]

821
59:14.615 --> 59:16.617
You'll die too if you stay here.

822
59:17.326 --> 59:18.410
Do as I say.

823
59:18.494 --> 59:20.204
Listen to me now.

824
59:21.246 --> 59:22.539
Just go!

825
59:24.375 --> 59:25.709
[screaming]

826
59:27.961 --> 59:29.463
Pyeongyeon Group killed my father!

827
59:29.546 --> 59:31.298
Pyeongyeon killed my dad.

828
59:32.216 --> 59:33.926
I said, Pyeongyeon killed my dad!

829
59:35.135 --> 59:36.887
Pyeongyeon killed my dad!

830
59:36.970 --> 59:38.389
[Han groaning]

831
59:39.431 --> 59:40.682
No.

832
59:41.975 --> 59:43.060
Not yet.

833
59:46.438 --> 59:47.606
Are you okay?

834
59:48.524 --> 59:50.567
[panting]

835
59:52.820 --> 59:53.862
Are you okay?

836
59:53.946 --> 59:55.614
[panting]

837
59:58.659 --> 59:59.660
Can you get up?

838
01:00:05.707 --> 01:00:07.084
[Han sighs]

839
01:00:26.019 --> 01:00:27.104
Are you okay?

840
01:00:30.816 --> 01:00:32.734
Do you know who I am?

841
01:00:39.741 --> 01:00:41.368
[news theme music playing]

842
01:00:45.664 --> 01:00:48.625
[Hae-seon on TV] The reason Pyeongyeon Group made the bold decision

843
01:00:48.709 --> 01:00:51.462
to abandon the outdated Plate In Asia system

844
01:00:51.545 --> 01:00:54.423
boils down to one concept.

845
01:00:54.506 --> 01:00:56.467
Returning to our roots.

846
01:00:57.176 --> 01:01:01.221
In the face of that spirit, authority, tradition and history mean nothing.

847
01:01:04.475 --> 01:01:06.351
From this very moment, we are going back

848
01:01:06.435 --> 01:01:08.896
to where we first began this eventful journey,

849
01:01:09.605 --> 01:01:11.023
back to where we searched

850
01:01:11.106 --> 01:01:14.193
for the finest Korean cuisine and the finest Korean chefs.

851
01:01:14.276 --> 01:01:17.154
We're leaving behind the system of scores and Plates to focus on people.

852
01:01:17.237 --> 01:01:18.655
We're casting off the shell

853
01:01:18.739 --> 01:01:21.241
to return to the essence of cooking.

854
01:01:25.370 --> 01:01:28.499
Ladies and gentlemen, this competition is not for Pyeongyeon Group.

855
01:01:28.582 --> 01:01:33.045
It is for our future and for our future of K-food on the world stage.

856
01:01:34.463 --> 01:01:37.257
The future of Korean cuisine is in your hands.

857
01:01:37.341 --> 01:01:41.720
Please, join us at The Table: K-Chef 2026.

858
01:01:46.850 --> 01:01:48.894
[pop song playing]

859
01:01:54.066 --> 01:01:55.859
[security guard] There he is! There he is!

860
01:01:55.943 --> 01:01:57.236
[security guard 2] Get him!

861
01:01:57.319 --> 01:01:58.946
Get him! Come on!

862
01:01:59.029 --> 01:02:00.614
[security guard 1] Run! Get him!

863
01:02:02.616 --> 01:02:04.493
Come on! Run!

864
01:02:05.160 --> 01:02:06.370
-Move! -Get him!

865
01:02:06.453 --> 01:02:09.706
He's just a kid! Come on. You're gonna let a kid outrun you?

866
01:02:09.790 --> 01:02:13.001
I'm trying! I'm trying! Come on!

867
01:02:14.002 --> 01:02:15.879
Come on! He's escaping!

868
01:02:21.301 --> 01:02:24.096
[pop music continues]

869
01:02:30.060 --> 01:02:31.645
[music ends]

870
01:02:40.445 --> 01:02:42.406
[music resumes]

871
01:03:12.394 --> 01:03:13.687
[Song-yi] Hey!

872
01:03:14.646 --> 01:03:16.064
Hey, wait, hold on.

873
01:03:16.982 --> 01:03:19.151
The boarding gates are that way.

874
01:03:35.751 --> 01:03:37.002
I'm in.

875
01:03:37.919 --> 01:03:40.005
What? [stammers] What do you…

876
01:03:40.088 --> 01:03:41.548
Let's do it.

877
01:03:42.424 --> 01:03:45.135
The Table: K-Chef 2026.

878
01:04:00.859 --> 01:04:03.779
[song continues playing]

879
01:04:31.473 --> 01:04:33.517
[Han] Cooking is about teamwork.

880
01:04:33.600 --> 01:04:34.726
That's not right.

881
01:04:34.810 --> 01:04:37.187
I've never cooked before, and I'm useless at it.

882
01:04:37.270 --> 01:04:39.731
The requirement is a team of four cooks.

883
01:04:39.815 --> 01:04:40.774
RÉSUMÉ

884
01:04:40.857 --> 01:04:42.943
Even if we start practicing around the clock right now,

885
01:04:43.026 --> 01:04:44.569
there's no guarantee we'll go far.

886
01:04:44.653 --> 01:04:48.323
The star of that show should be actually someone that we cast.

887
01:04:49.324 --> 01:04:51.702
[Woo-jin] I figured it'd just be a bunch of hacks turning up,

888
01:04:51.785 --> 01:04:53.829
but this looks fun.

889
01:04:53.912 --> 01:04:57.416
-Camera rolling -[host] Let the competition begin!

890
01:04:57.499 --> 01:04:59.167
[Han] Because in the end,

891
01:04:59.876 --> 01:05:01.628
you'll lose to me again.
